jobs.description:
Robert Half is currently looking for a Receptionist (m/f/x).

The company is located in Brussels and this is a full-time position within a legal services environment.

The responsibilities of this position as Receptionist are:

• Welcoming clients, visitors and business partners in a professional and courteous manner;
• Managing incoming calls and ensuring enquiries are efficiently directed to the appropriate person;
• Preparing meeting rooms and contributing to a smooth, welcoming and professional client experience;
• Coordinating incoming and outgoing mail, courier services and deliveries;
• Providing administrative support, including document handling, filing, archiving and printing;
• Monitoring office supplies and liaising with suppliers when necessary;
• Helping maintain an organised, professional and pleasant working environment;
• Providing practical support to colleagues and contributing to the efficient day-to-day running of the office;
• Working closely with the morning receptionist to ensure continuity throughout the day and foster good collaboration within the team.


The required qualifications for this position as Receptionist are:

• You have a very good command of Dutch, French and English;
• You have a good knowledge of Office 365;
• You are customer-oriented and enjoy interacting with different people;
• You take ownership and proactively look for solutions;
• You are organised and have a strong eye for detail;
• You remain calm and efficient when priorities change;
• You are reliable, discreet and professional;
• You enjoy working in a dynamic environment and are a strong team player.

Your role



• Deal with all aspects of border compliance & customs related activities in the Shipping & Port environment where the objectives are to ensure Compliance with applicable legislation and maximising the efficient flow of goods by resolving any issue that may occur; 

• Liaise with Port and Customs authorities, including obtaining & maintaining the necessary authorisations (AEO, Bonded Warehouse, Temporary Storage, etc...); 

• Centre of expertise for Customs matters for the organization serving internal & external stakeholders; 

• Creating, maintaining & delivering organisation wide procedures, KPI’s and reports ; 

• Continuously seeking to improve our operation & systems. 

Your profile



• You are fluent in English.  Any additional language is an advantage; 

• Ideally, you have relevant experience or knowledge in Shipping, Ports or Customs but more importantly a willingness to learn a large amount of complicated subject matter in a short timeframe; 

• You are passionate and fast learner with a hands-on, problem solving mentality that doesn’t relent until an issue is resolved; 

• You have excellent communication skills and the ability to create solid relations with both internal and external clients and partners; 

• You are able to prioritise, work autonomously and always seek improvements; 

• Once every 12 weeks, you provide a standby cover to ensure our operations are supported at all times (Weekend – Early evening). 

• You meet the criteria for obtaining a legally required positive safety assessment for critical roles in the port.
